{
  "theorem_discrete": "Conditioned on an event schedule with M hidden reset events whose q-state targets must be independent uniform symbols, any globally invertible implementation needs hidden content entropy at least M log2(q), hence at least q^M distinguishable hidden content states.",
  "poisson_mean_bound": "For n sites, local hidden reset rate alpha*rho per site and horizon T, E[H_hidden_content | schedule count] >= alpha*n*rho*T*log2(q) bits.",
  "pure_swap_alpha0": "Requires no fresh target-symbol entropy beyond the controller/event schedule because each event is a permutation of already visible record contents.",
  "scope_warning": "This compares fresh content entropy conditional on the same declared event schedule. Pure SWAP still requires a reversible account of event/controller randomness. The theorem selects alpha=0 only under a global-closure/minimal-hidden-content principle.",
